[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5397541451","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122711#issuecomment-5397541451","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122711","id":5397541451,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQbfySw","user":{"login":"Synzorasize","id":60207816,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMjA3ODE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60207816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize","html_url":"https://github.com/Synzorasize","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Synzorasize/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T15:33:53Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T15:33:53Z","body":"> I think you are missing an edge case. If a not abstract script inherits from an abstract native type it can be attached to an instance of that native type, but constructing it with `new()` makes no sense.\r\n\r\nI forgot that it was possible to extend an abstract class while it still not being constructible (it _is_ an edge case). So this means that all ancestral classes have to be checked in `is_constructible_object`. Idk how complex that'll be but I'll see what can be done.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5397541451/reactions","total_count":0,"+1"